{"1-8":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H3684","lemma":"כְּסִיל","tr":"ke·sil","gloss":"fool","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":70},{"base":"H6310","lemma":"פֶּה","tr":"peh","gloss":"lip","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":498},{"base":"H8193","lemma":"שָׂפָה","tr":"sa·phah","gloss":"lips","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":176},{"base":"H7563","lemma":"רָשָׁע","tr":"ra·sah","gloss":"wicked","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":263},{"base":"H3859","lemma":"לָהַם","tr":"la·ham","gloss":"to swallow","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H4112","lemma":"מַהֲלֻמֿוֹת","tr":"ma·ha·lum·mah","gloss":"blow","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H1566","lemma":"גָּלַע","tr":"ga·la","gloss":"to quarrel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H7279","lemma":"רָגַן","tr":"ra·gan","gloss":"to grumble","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H0937","lemma":"בּוּז","tr":"buz","gloss":"contempt","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"H4288","lemma":"מְחִתָּה","tr":"me·chit·tah","gloss":"terror","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EPH","chapter":5,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":19,"source":"openbible","text":"Pay careful attention, then, to how you walk, not as unwise but as wise,","from":1},{"book":"EPH","chapter":5,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":19,"source":"openbible","text":"Therefore do not be foolish, but understand what the Lordʼs will is.","from":1},{"book":"PRO","chapter":1,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"The fear of the LORD is the beginning of knowledge, but fools despise wisdom and discipline.","from":2},{"book":"PRO","chapter":2,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"My son, if you accept my words and hide my commandments within you,","from":1},{"book":"PRO","chapter":2,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"For the LORD gives wisdom; from His mouth come knowledge and understanding.","from":1},{"book":"PRO","chapter":20,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"It is honorable for a man to resolve a dispute, but any fool will quarrel.","from":1},{"book":"PRO","chapter":12,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"A shrewd man keeps his knowledge to himself, but a foolish heart proclaims its folly.","from":2},{"book":"PRO","chapter":13,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"He who guards his mouth protects his life, but the one who opens his lips invites his own ruin.","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"9-17":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H7682","lemma":"שָׂגַב","tr":"sa·gav","gloss":"to exalt","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":20},{"base":"H1847","lemma":"דַּ֫עַת","tr":"da·at","gloss":"knowledge","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":92},{"base":"H5797","lemma":"עֹז","tr":"oz","gloss":"strength","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":92},{"base":"H6662","lemma":"צַדִּיק","tr":"tsad·diq","gloss":"righteous","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":206},{"base":"H7307","lemma":"רוּחַ","tr":"ru·ach","gloss":"spirit","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":378},{"base":"H5218","lemma":"נָכָא","tr":"na·ka","gloss":"stricken","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H4976","lemma":"מַתָּן","tr":"mat·tan","gloss":"gift","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H6038","lemma":"עֲנָוָה","tr":"a·na·vah","gloss":"humility","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H3820","lemma":"לֵב","tr":"lev","gloss":"heart","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":595},{"base":"H4245","lemma":"מַחֲלֶה","tr":"ma·cha·leh","gloss":"sickness","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2SA","chapter":22,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":73,"source":"both","text":"My God is my rock, in whom I take refuge, my shield, and the horn of my salvation. My stronghold, my refuge, and my Savior, You save me from violence.","from":10},{"book":"PSA","chapter":91,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":66,"source":"both","text":"I will say to the LORD, “You are my refuge and my fortress, my God, in whom I trust.”","from":10},{"book":"ISA","chapter":26,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":60,"source":"both","text":"Trust in the LORD forever, because GOD the LORD is the Rock eternal.","from":10},{"book":"PSA","chapter":144,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":43,"source":"both","text":"He is my steadfast love and my fortress, my stronghold and my deliverer. He is my shield, in whom I take refuge, who subdues peoples under me.","from":10},{"book":"PSA","chapter":61,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":40,"source":"openbible","text":"For You have been my refuge, a tower of strength against the enemy.","from":10},{"book":"PSA","chapter":61,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":40,"source":"openbible","text":"Let me dwell in Your tent forever and take refuge in the shelter of Your wings. Selah","from":10},{"book":"PSA","chapter":27,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":30,"source":"both","text":"The LORD is my light and my salvation— whom shall I fear? The LORD is the stronghold of my life— whom shall I dread?","from":10},{"book":"GEN","chapter":17,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":26,"source":"both","text":"When Abram was ninety-nine years old, the Lordappeared to him and said, “I am God Almighty. Walk before Me and be blameless.","from":10}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"18-24":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H4079","lemma":"מִדְיָן","tr":"mid·yan","gloss":"contention","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":10},{"base":"H7646","lemma":"שָׂבֵעַ","tr":"sa·va","gloss":"to satisfy","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":97},{"base":"H6529","lemma":"פְּרִי","tr":"pe·ri","gloss":"fruit","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":119},{"base":"H0157","lemma":"אָהֵב","tr":"a·hav","gloss":"to love: lover","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":211},{"base":"H1695","lemma":"דָּבֵק","tr":"da·veq","gloss":"cleaving","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H4672","lemma":"מָצָא","tr":"ma·tsa","gloss":"to find","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":455},{"base":"H0251","lemma":"אָח","tr":"ach","gloss":"brother: male-sibling","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":629},{"base":"H6329","lemma":"פּוּק","tr":"puq","gloss":"to promote","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H8469","lemma":"תַּחֲנוּן","tr":"ta·cha·nun","gloss":"supplication","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":18},{"base":"H6223","lemma":"עָשִׁיר","tr":"a·shir","gloss":"rich","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":23}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EPH","chapter":4,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":144,"source":"both","text":"Let no unwholesome talk come out of your mouths, but only what is helpful for building up the one in need and bringing grace to those who listen.","from":21},{"book":"MAT","chapter":12,"verse":35,"verseEnd":35,"votes":129,"source":"openbible","text":"The good man brings good things out of his good store of treasure, and the evil man brings evil things out of his evil store of treasure.","from":21},{"book":"MAT","chapter":12,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":129,"source":"openbible","text":"For by your words you will be acquitted, and by your words you will be condemned.”","from":21},{"book":"COL","chapter":4,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":109,"source":"both","text":"Let your speech always be gracious, seasoned with salt, so that you may know how to answer everyone.","from":21},{"book":"PRO","chapter":10,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":92,"source":"both","text":"When words are many, sin is unavoidable, but he who restrains his lips is wise.","from":21},{"book":"PRO","chapter":10,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":92,"source":"openbible","text":"The lips of the righteous feed many, but fools die for lack of judgment.","from":21},{"book":"JAS","chapter":3,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":86,"source":"openbible","text":"The tongue also is a fire, a world of wickedness among the parts of the body. It pollutes the whole person, sets the course of his life on fire, and is itself set on fire by hell.","from":21},{"book":"JAS","chapter":3,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":86,"source":"openbible","text":"With the tongue we bless our Lord and Father, and with it we curse men, who have been made in Godʼs likeness.","from":21}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}